WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.176
The feature, and the mistake to avoid.

2
00:00:02.456 --> 00:00:14.381
The Studio 1 project is a tool that takes a meeting transcript and produces action items: what needs doing, who owns it, when it is due, and the words in the meeting that prove someone committed to it.

3
00:00:14.661 --> 00:00:18.992
A person reviews the list, and only approved items reach a task tracker.

4
00:00:19.272 --> 00:00:23.027
The tempting first version is one prompt: “Here is a transcript.

5
00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:25.355
List the action items as JSON.

6
00:00:25.635 --> 00:00:29.837
” It will produce something plausible on the first try, and that is the danger.

7
00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:34.363
Lesson 1 warned that fluent output is not evidence of correctness.

8
00:00:34.643 --> 00:00:47.571
A single prompt gives you no place to check anything: if an owner is wrong, you cannot tell whether the model misheard the transcript, guessed between two people with the same first name, or invented the item entirely.

9
00:00:47.851 --> 00:00:50.133
This lesson lays out a design instead.

10
00:00:50.413 --> 00:00:55.597
Each stage has one job, produces output you can inspect, and is followed by a check.

11
00:00:55.877 --> 00:01:00.229
It is not the only valid design, and the project leaves the details to you.

12
00:01:00.509 --> 00:01:06.611
But every choice below is one you should be able to defend with the concepts from lessons 1 through 11.
